---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import siteConfig from '../config/site';

const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL.replace(/\/$/, '');
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Privacy Policy | K-Pop Hangul"
  description="Privacy Policy and data practices for the K-Pop Hangul educational website."
>
  <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8 py-16">
    <div class="bg-white p-8 sm:p-12 rounded-3xl border border-slate-200/80 shadow-sm prose prose-slate max-w-none text-sm leading-relaxed">
      <h1 class="text-2xl sm:text-3xl font-extrabold text-slate-900 tracking-tight mb-2">Privacy Policy</h1>
      <p class="text-slate-400 text-xs mb-8">Last Updated: September 2026</p>

      <p>
        At <strong>{siteConfig.site.name}</strong> ("we", "our", or "us"), accessible from <a href={siteConfig.site.url}>{siteConfig.site.url}</a>, the privacy of our visitors is of paramount importance. This Privacy Policy document outlines the types of information collected and recorded by K-Pop Hangul and how we use it.
      </p>

      <h2>1. Information We Collect</h2>
      <p>
        K-Pop Hangul is an educational static website (JAMstack). We do not require account registration, and we do not store sensitive personal passwords or payment details on our servers.
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Log Files & Analytics</strong>: Like most modern websites, K-Pop Hangul uses standard log files and privacy-focused traffic analytics (e.g., Google Analytics 4) to monitor site health, browser types, referral sources, and page popularity. This data is aggregated and cannot be used to personally identify individual visitors.</li>
        <li><strong>Direct Communications</strong>: If you contact us directly via email or our contact form, we may receive your name, email address, and message contents for the sole purpose of responding to your inquiry.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>2. Cookies & Web Beacons</h2>
      <p>
        K-Pop Hangul uses essential cookies to store user preferences (such as light/dark mode settings and client-side flashcard states) and optimize page delivery speeds via Content Delivery Networks (CDNs).
      </p>

      <h2>3. Third-Party Advertising & Services</h2>
      <p>
        Our website may partner with third-party service providers (such as Google AdSense or analytical platforms) that use cookies and JavaScript to deliver relevant educational resources or advertisements:
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li>Third-party ad vendors, including Google, use cookies to serve ads based on a user's prior visits to this website or other websites.</li>
        <li>Users may opt out of personalized advertising by visiting <a href="https://adssettings.google.com/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="text-indigo-600 underline">Google Ads Settings</a> or <a href="https://www.aboutads.info" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="text-indigo-600 underline">aboutads.info</a>.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>4. External Audio & Video Embeds</h2>
      <p>
        Our lessons may reference official music videos and audio snippets via YouTube, Spotify, or Melon. Interacting with embedded players or external music widgets is governed by the respective platform's privacy policies.
      </p>

      <h2>5. Children's Information</h2>
      <p>
        K-Pop Hangul does not knowingly collect any Personal Identifiable Information from children under the age of 13. If you think that your child provided this kind of information on our website, we strongly encourage you to contact us immediately, and we will do our best efforts to promptly remove such information.
      </p>

      <h2>6. Contacting Us</h2>
      <p>
        If you have questions or require more information about our Privacy Policy, do not hesitate to contact us through our <a href={`${base}/contact/`} class="text-indigo-600 underline font-medium">Contact Page</a>.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>

